IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dom-rules`

-- Domicile Act 1982 (Cth) — the encoder's tests.

§ `Tests`

-- An adult of 30, never married, residing in the country with the intention.
adult MEANS
    `Domicile case` OF Date 1 1 2020, Date 1 1 1990, FALSE, FALSE,
                       `with neither parent`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, `not adopted`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

GIVEN t IS A DATE, b IS A DATE, w IS A BOOLEAN, h IS A `Principal home`, sep IS A BOOLEAN, o IS A BOOLEAN, ad IS AN `Adoption`, r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Domicile case`
`a case at` t `born` b `married` w `home` h `apart` sep `other parent` o `adoption` ad `rescinded` r MEANS
    `Domicile case` OF t, b, w, FALSE, h, sep, o, FALSE, ad, r, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

-- s 8: 18 on the birthday.
#ASSERT `may I have a domicile of my own` adult EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `may I have a domicile of my own` (`a case at` (Date 1 1 2008) `born` (Date 1 1 1990) `married` FALSE `home` `with both of my parents` `apart` FALSE `other parent` TRUE `adoption` `not adopted` `rescinded` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `may I have a domicile of my own` (`a case at` (Date 31 12 2007) `born` (Date 1 1 1990) `married` FALSE `home` `with both of my parents` `apart` FALSE `other parent` TRUE `adoption` `not adopted` `rescinded` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 8(1)(b): a married 17-year-old.
#ASSERT `may I have a domicile of my own` (`a case at` (Date 31 12 2007) `born` (Date 1 1 1990) `married` TRUE `home` `with both of my parents` `apart` FALSE `other parent` TRUE `adoption` `not adopted` `rescinded` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 5(1): before 1 July 1982.
#ASSERT `may I have a domicile of my own` (`a case at` (Date 30 6 1982) `born` (Date 1 1 1950) `married` FALSE `home` `with neither parent` `apart` FALSE `other parent` TRUE `adoption` `not adopted` `rescinded` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 8(2)
#ASSERT `may I have a domicile of my own` (`Domicile case` OF Date 1 1 2020, Date 1 1 1990, FALSE, TRUE, `with neither parent`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, `not adopted`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 9(1)
#ASSERT `whose domicile I take as a child` (`a case at` (Date 1 1 2020) `born` (Date 1 1 2010) `married` FALSE `home` `with one of my parents` `apart` TRUE `other parent` TRUE `adoption` `not adopted` `rescinded` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the domicile the parent I live with has from time to time`
#ASSERT `whose domicile I take as a child` (`a case at` (Date 1 1 2020) `born` (Date 1 1 2010) `married` FALSE `home` `with one of my parents` `apart` FALSE `other parent` FALSE `adoption` `not adopted` `rescinded` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the domicile the parent I live with has from time to time`
-- s 9(3)(b): parents living together; the common law governs.
#ASSERT `whose domicile I take as a child` (`a case at` (Date 1 1 2020) `born` (Date 1 1 2010) `married` FALSE `home` `with both of my parents` `apart` FALSE `other parent` TRUE `adoption` `not adopted` `rescinded` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 9(2)
#ASSERT `whose domicile I take as a child` (`a case at` (Date 1 1 2020) `born` (Date 1 1 2010) `married` FALSE `home` `with both of my parents` `apart` FALSE `other parent` TRUE `adoption` `adopted by 2 parents` `rescinded` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the domicile I would have if born in wedlock to my adoptive parents`
#ASSERT `whose domicile I take as a child` (`a case at` (Date 1 1 2020) `born` (Date 1 1 2010) `married` FALSE `home` `with neither parent` `apart` FALSE `other parent` FALSE `adoption` `adopted by 1 parent only` `rescinded` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the domicile my sole adoptive parent has from time to time`
-- s 9(5)
#ASSERT `whose domicile I take as a child` (`a case at` (Date 1 1 2020) `born` (Date 1 1 2010) `married` FALSE `home` `with neither parent` `apart` FALSE `other parent` FALSE `adoption` `adopted by 1 parent only` `rescinded` TRUE) EQUALS JUST `as the rescission order provides, otherwise as if I had not been adopted`
-- not a child
#ASSERT `whose domicile I take as a child` adult EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 10
#ASSERT `have I acquired a domicile of choice` adult EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `have I acquired a domicile of choice` (`Domicile case` OF Date 1 1 2020, Date 1 1 1990, FALSE, FALSE, `with neither parent`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, `not adopted`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a child cannot
#ASSERT `have I acquired a domicile of choice` (`Domicile case` OF Date 1 1 2020, Date 1 1 2010, FALSE, FALSE, `with neither parent`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, `not adopted`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 9(4)
#ASSERT `do I keep my domicile from childhood` (`Domicile case` OF Date 1 1 2020, Date 1 1 2001, FALSE, FALSE, `with neither parent`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, `not adopted`, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `do I keep my domicile from childhood` (`Domicile case` OF Date 1 1 2020, Date 1 1 2001, FALSE, FALSE, `with neither parent`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, `not adopted`, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ss 6-7
#ASSERT `does my domicile follow my husband's` adult EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `does my domicile of origin revive` adult EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`the domicile position for` adult)'s `I may have a domicile of my own` EQUALS JUST TRUE
